{"id":"fca41b32-863f-479b-aa15-7ec7e1309d31","object":"chat.completion","created":1788899776,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"The failing argument is the `parseBearer(authorization)` arm — the checker doesn't narrow `authorization` through the ternary condition. I'll restructure to early-return guards, which the durable example shows the checker narrows correctly.","reasoning_content":"ZTS203: argument type does not match: expected string, got string | undefined. Which argument? Possibly parseBearer's param expects string, but authorization narrowed... Actually we guarded `authorization === undefined ? undefined : parseBearer(authorization)`. Hmm — does the ternary narrow `authorization` in the else branch? Maybe the checker doesn't narrow through the ternary condition on `authorization === undefined`. Or the issue is `env("JWT_SECRET")` is `string?`... jwtVerify expects secret: string? Signature says jwtVerify(token, secret, ...) returns Result — token is string, secret string presumably. After `if (secret === undefined) return`, secret should be narrowed to string in the rest. But narrowing may not persist after jwtVerify? That call appears after the check.

