But this ZigTS type checker may have restriction: ZTS624 etc. Maybe the ternary condition `authorization === undefined ? undefined : parseBearer(authorization)` — parseBearer param expects string; in the false-branch the checker should treat authorization as string. Maybe the checker unions labels through comparison and doesn't narrow in ternary branches; similar note in the durable example: "The presence test `approval !== undefined` does not narrow that". So comparisons don't narrow non-local values? Actually the durable note says presence test `approval !== undefined` does not narrow unknown. So narrow works only in if-statement? They use `if (key === undefined)` then `return` then later use key — maybe that narrowed... The durable example did use `if (key === undefined) return ...;` then used key in signal(key,...). So if-statement narrowing works for string? maybe.

So which argument failed, string | undefined expected string? Could be `jwtVerify(token, secret)` where token is string|undefined because the token value came from ternary where parseBearer returns string?; parseBearer returns `string?` per catalog! Yes: parseBearer(authorizationHeader): string?. So token is `string | undefined`, then we check `if (token === undefined) return`... then jwtVerify(token, secret) after that check, token narrowed to string. Hmm.

